# Backend Reactive Threading

Before writing or reviewing a `Mono` or `Flux` chain, load the `reactive-threading` skill and run its "Validate" steps.

- A blocking call (I/O that returns a plain value: S3, JDBI, sync Redisson, `@Cacheable` getters, sync HTTP) runs in
  its own `Offload.blocking(...)`.
- CPU that grows with the input runs in `Offload.cpu(...)`, never on `boundedElastic` or a client thread.
- Never block on `ClickHouseWorker`, `chc-operation`, `redisson-netty` or `parallel`; `block()` only at the edge.
- Light work gets no hop.
